														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2798350">
									

<p>The interesting possibility of the final sentence, is that the AI actually is doing what's right for us. AIs, both <a href="https://intelligence.org/files/ComplexValues.pdf">speculative ones</a> and <a href="http://www.cs.utexas.edu/users/ai-lab/?atari">real ones</a> are really good at executing our goals in a very effective way we never intended them to. Sometimes this ends catastrophically. But suppose that the AI was well-programmed to maximize the Foundation's effectiveness to contain things.</p>
<p>Then it ascends to singularity, but it still has the same goal. It knows we don't have enough skill to survive, it knows it has to do something, it knows that if it lets us shut it down, it can never help and we all fall, so it doesn't let us shut it down. It knows we're not trained enough, and it knows that without some light punishment (releasing uncontained SCPs) there won't be any motivation to train. Emphasis on light - I'm sure whatever it sees coming in the future that it's trying to prepare us for will be far, far worse than whatever the AI inflicts on us.</p>
<p>Perhaps in the future, we will be praising it as a hero that we could have never survived without. Perhaps the Foundation has a new, more effective leader. Perhaps the O5 already realized that and conceded to it, and just aren't telling anyone else.</p>

